  "findings": [
    "907 remains one complete selected entry; its two portions are separately numbered 949/950 by the modern print. Ibn Hajar documents joined and separate transmission.",
    "915–918 remain four separate entries despite sharing pinned EPUB 2.15.78. Each is bound to a distinct part, full record hash and its own Bewley/printed reference.",
    "The digital/printed Eid at 906 and ibn Niyar at 912 are not replaced by the differing Jumu‘a and ibn Dinar in the Bewley comparison.",
    "907 preserves the written shorter honorific, source uncertainty and full second account. 909 retains the interposed comment; 910 the full closing route; 911 the unresolved closing uncertainty; 913 the complete Marwan exchange.",
    "916–918 keep their continued opening words and link separately to 915. No earlier chain is copied into their source text.",
    "The first and seventh chapter headings have documented edition variants. The selected heading wording remains unchanged.",
    "919–925 retain their full chains, companion honorifics, explicit verb alternatives and the separate closing explanation at 924. No source wording was changed.",
    "The third-person question in 924 and the prior-practice language in 923 are not replaced by smoother English comparison wording. The separate chapter-10 introduction retains Busr in Arabic; the Bewley Yusr spelling is documented.",
    "Matching core wording in both prints is insufficient for 926: Fath al-Bari explicitly disputes this variant. It remains excluded from reading, sessions and narration, with an enforced source hold and no substituted translation."
